# DERIVED FILES ARE NEVER MERGED TEXTUALLY.
#
# Each of these is rebuilt from other committed content by
# tools/regen_derived.sh. Two branches that each regenerate one rewrite the
# same aggregate lines - "531 artifacts, 594 arms", a summary block, a
# source_structural_sha256 - so ANY pair of such branches conflicts, every
# time, on lines that carry no information. That cost five CI failures and
# repeated manual resolution in two days.
#
# `merge=ours` takes this side without conflicting; the post-merge and
# post-rewrite hooks then rebuild the file from the merged tree, which is the
# only correct content. BOTH HALVES ARE REQUIRED. Without the driver git stops
# on a meaningless conflict; without the hooks the merge silently keeps a stale
# file, which is worse. Install both with tools/install_git_hooks.sh.
#
# A custom merge driver that regenerates cannot replace this. Measured
# 2026-08-20: git runs merge drivers BEFORE the other side's files reach the
# working tree, so the driver rebuilt from a tree missing the very artifacts
# being merged and produced an index silently short one entry.
RESULTS_INDEX.md                                merge=ours
results_index.csv                               merge=ours
LEGACY_ATTRIBUTION_AUDIT_2026-08-05.md          merge=ours
ab_test_runtime/audit/*.json                    merge=ours
app/tests/unit_test_inventory.json              merge=ours
